# Resident-cap proof image: stressprobe on a real-disk KRFFS.
#
# Built into a partitioned disk by mkdisk.sh and booted with rach2.fsdisk +
# rach2.rescue. The debug shell runs `exec /stressprobe`, which writes and
# re-reads 33 MiB of files (past the 32 MiB physical-RAM cap) through the 4 MiB
# cache, proving an on-disk file system larger than memory round-trips.
file 0755 /stressprobe build/tests/stressprobe
